# Normalise line endings so a fresh checkout formats identically on every OS.
#
# Without this, Git converts LF to CRLF when checking out on Windows, and
# `biome check` then reports every file as needing reformatting. The authoring
# worktree passes (its files were written with LF) while a clean clone fails —
# and a Linux CI runner passes while a Windows machine fails. Pinning eol=lf
# makes the formatter's view of the tree identical everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

